  "overview": {
    "text": "Austin is Texas’s capital and the seat of Travis County, situated in Central Texas along the Colorado River near the eastern edge of the Hill Country. The Republic of Texas selected the Waterloo settlement for a planned capital in 1839, renaming it for Stephen F. Austin, a prominent early Texas leader. Its setting and role were disputed: opponents considered the site remote, and political conflict temporarily displaced the government in 1842; it returned in 1845. After Texas joined the United States, Austin became the state capital in 1846. The city’s identity grew around government and education, including the University of Texas, selected for Austin in 1881. At its core, the historic street grid leads toward the Capitol from the river.",
    "source_urls": [
      "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/austin-tx-travis-county",
      "https://www.tsl.texas.gov/treasures/republic/archwar/archwar.html",
      "https://www.tspb.texas.gov/prop/tc/tc-history/history/index.html"
    ]
  },
  "key_facts": [
    {
      "text": "Austin’s original town plan was a grid between Waller Creek and Shoal Creek, with Congress Avenue connecting the Colorado River to Capitol Square.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/austin-tx-travis-county"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Texas government moved away in 1842 amid conflict over the Republic’s archives and returned to Austin in 1845.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/austin-tx-travis-county",
        "https://www.tsl.texas.gov/treasures/republic/archwar/archwar.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1850, Texans voted to keep Austin as the state capital.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/austin-tx-travis-county",
        "https://www.tsl.texas.gov/treasures/republic/archwar/archwar.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The University of Texas chose Austin as the site for its main university in 1881; instruction began two years later.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/austin-tx-travis-county"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The present Texas Capitol was dedicated in 1888, linking the city’s government role with a prominent landmark.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/austin-tx-travis-county",
        "https://www.tspb.texas.gov/prop/tc/tc-history/history/index.html"
      ]
    }
  ],
